---

KoboldCpp doesn't come with an AI model; you add one. A model is one large file that ends in `.gguf`.

## The easy way: a newbie template

A template fills in the launcher for you and downloads the model when you click **Launch**. The `Chatbot` templates also add voice input, read-aloud and picture understanding.

{% steps %}

1. In the launcher, click **Get Help**. **Newbie Templates** is already selected.

2. Pick a template for your graphics card's memory (VRAM; [how to check](/download/#which-graphics-card-do-i-have)):

   - `LowSpec-Chatbot`: for about 6 GB. Also pick it with less, or without a graphics card; it then runs slower. Downloads about 4 GB.
   - `MidSpec-Chatbot`: for about 12 GB or more. Downloads about 7 GB.

   The other templates make pictures, music or video, or run a coding agent.

3. Click **Load Template**.

   ![The Help Menu: Newbie Templates, the LowSpec-Chatbot template and the Load Template button](../../../assets/docs/getting-started/launcher-get-help.png)

{% /steps %}

## Or: download one model file

These are the models the KoboldCpp README recommends. Click one to download it.

{% cardgrid %}
{% linkcard title="Qwen3-VL-8B" description="The best all-rounder · 4.8 GB" href="https://huggingface.co/unsloth/Qwen3-VL-8B-Instruct-GGUF/resolve/main/Qwen3-VL-8B-Instruct-Q4_K_S.gguf" /%}
{% linkcard title="L3-8B-Stheno-v3.2" description="Creative writing and roleplay · 4.7 GB" href="https://huggingface.co/bartowski/L3-8B-Stheno-v3.2-GGUF/resolve/main/L3-8B-Stheno-v3.2-Q4_K_S.gguf" /%}
{% linkcard title="Gemma 3 4B" description="Small and fast, for weaker PCs · 2.5 GB" href="https://huggingface.co/ggml-org/gemma-3-4b-it-GGUF/resolve/main/gemma-3-4b-it-Q4_K_M.gguf" /%}
{% linkcard title="PicX Real" description="Makes pictures · 1.7 GB" href="https://huggingface.co/koboldcpp/imgmodel/resolve/main/picx_real_q5_1.gguf" /%}
{% /cardgrid %}

In the launcher, click **Browse** next to **GGUF Text Model:** and select the file. PicX Real is an image model: it goes into **Image Model:** on the **Image Gen** tab instead.

## Launch

Click **Launch**.

![GGUF Text Model field with a model selected (1) and the Launch button (2)](../../../assets/docs/getting-started/launcher-model-launch.png)

The launcher closes, and the console window shows the model loading. With a template, it first downloads the files, which can take a while. The next launch reuses them.
